overload64.t failures The recent smoke tests show failures on some configurations with
-Duselongdoubles or -Dusemorebits for the new test lib/overload64.t.
(See smoke reports by Merijn and Johan.)

I can't duplicate those failures for now (on a FreeBSD box, with
-Duse64bitint). However it looks like those tests should be skipped.
Currently the test file begins with:

    if ($Config::Config{'uvsize'} != 8) {
        print "1..0 # Skip -- Perl configured with 32-bit ints\\n";
        exit 0;
    }

Maybe that needs to be changed. t/op/64bitint.t for example uses:

        eval { my $q = pack "q", 0 };
        if ($@) {
                print "1..0 # Skip: no 64-bit types\\n";
                exit(0);
        }

although I'm not sure that's completely equivalent.

